{
  "id": "corporate-flight-bookings",
  "questionId": "corporate-flight-bookings",
  "slug": "corporate-flight-bookings",
  "title": "Corporate Flight Bookings",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Prefix sum",
  "patterns": [
    "prefix sum",
    "difference array"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "adding the same value to an entire range, many times, is expensive if done range by range. what if you only marked where a range's effect BEGINS and ENDS?",
    "for a booking [first, last, seats], add seats at position first-1, and subtract seats at position last (just past the range, 0-indexed)",
    "do this for every booking into a difference array of length n, without touching the interior of any range",
    "finally, take a running prefix sum over the difference array - each position accumulates exactly the seats that apply to it"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "off-by-one converting between the 1-indexed booking range and a 0-indexed array",
    "forgetting to subtract at last (not last - 1), since the subtraction should take effect the flight AFTER the range ends",
    "applying the seats directly to every flight in the range instead of using the start/end marking trick, missing the efficiency gain"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are `n` flights, numbered 1 to `n`. You're given a list of\n`bookings`, where each booking is [first, last, seats] meaning seats\nseats were reserved on every flight from first to last, inclusive\n(1-indexed).\n\n**Return an array of length `n` where position i holds the total number of seats reserved on flight i+1.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= n <= 2 * 10^4",
      "1 <= bookings.length <= 2 * 10^4",
      "bookings[i].length == 3",
      "1 <= first_i <= last_i <= n",
      "1 <= seats_i <= 10^6"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a single booking covering the entire range",
      "many bookings overlapping the same flight",
      "a booking covering only one flight (first equals last)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
